Subject: [PATCH 42/42] feat(hackberrypi): ship stock Waydroid

Deckard M0 runs Android apps under Marathon's compositor through stock
Waydroid on the HackberryPi. The image gets waydroid and waydroid-systemd
(lxc, gbinder-python, dnsmasq and iptables come in as dependencies).

Nothing else is needed at the image level. waydroid-container.service is
D-Bus activated by "waydroid session start", and Waydroid mounts
binderfs and allocates its binder nodes itself. The Android system and
vendor images (about 2.4 GB) are downloaded by "waydroid init" on the
device, not baked in. The iptables modules Android's netd needs come
from device-hackberrypi-cm5-marathon.

Findings and the commands used: docs/testing/DECKARD_M0_HACKBERRYPI.md
in Marathon-Shell.
---
 scripts/mkosi-configure.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/mkosi-configure.py b/scripts/mkosi-configure.py
index ee6b7a0..46b8d80 100755
--- a/scripts/mkosi-configure.py
+++ b/scripts/mkosi-configure.py
@@ -162,6 +162,8 @@ def main() -> int:
             )
             if has_hbp:
                 extra_overlays.append(hbp)
+                # Deckard M0: stock Waydroid (docs/testing/DECKARD_M0_HACKBERRYPI.md).
+                extra_overlays.extend(["waydroid", "waydroid-systemd"])
         config["Packages"] = list(dict.fromkeys(existing + dynamic + extra_overlays))
     elif image == "default-initrd":
         # pmaports emits InitrdPackages to distinguish base-image pkgs from
